\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{One exterior product and two bilinear orders}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For #{F=k^2} with dual basis #{e^1,e^2}, the area
covector #{\beta=e^1\wedge e^2} gives the
[exterior insertion](fdip-00WU)
#{P_{\beta,x}=\psi_{x,1}\psi_{x,2}}.
Its associated alternating bilinear form is
#{b(v,w)=v_1w_2-v_2w_1}. Substituting the same odd field
into both arguments gives
##{b(\psi_x,\psi_x)
 =\psi_{x,1}\psi_{x,2}-\psi_{x,2}\psi_{x,1}
 =2\psi_{x,1}\psi_{x,2}.}
Over a nonzero ring of characteristic two this full
contraction is zero, while the exterior insertion remains
a basis vector. The exterior insertion is therefore
defined by its covector, without division by two.}
